  partName: Top Front Stud
  description: The Top Front Stud is a tiny, thin-flat stud situated at the top-center-front
    of the engine, made of Material.006, which serves as a threaded fastener for
    various components. This stud provides a secure mounting point for parts such
    as the top front cover plate or sensors, and an interesting detail is that it
    often features a specialized coating to prevent corrosion and ensure a reliable
    connection. The Top Front Stud plays a critical role in maintaining the engine's
    overall structure and performance.
  audioExplanation: {fileID: 0}
